\label{thm: stable family birational boundedness}
    Let $d$ be a positive integer. Then there exists a number $t=t(d)\in(0,1)$ depending only on $d$ with the following property.


    Assume that $f\colon X\to T$ is a stable family of maximal variation such that $X$ is normal and projective, and $\dim X=d$. Then:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $K_{t}:=tK_{X/T}+(1-t)K_X$ is big.
        \item Assume that $\operatorname{vol}(K_t)\leq C$ for some constant $C$. Then $X$ is birationally bounded.
    \end{enumerate}

