\label{conj: acc interpolated}
Let $d$ be a positive integer. Then there exists an ACC set $\Gamma\subset [0,1]$ depending only on $d$ such that for any $\mathbb Q$-Gorenstein foliation $\mathcal{F}$ on a $\mathbb Q$-Gorenstein variety $X$, the interpolated log canonical (lc) threshold
\[
\operatorname{lct}(X;\mathcal{F}):=\sup\{t\geq 0\mid (X,\mathcal{F},t)\text{ is log canonical}\}
\]
belongs to $\Gamma$.

