    Let $d$ be a positive integer and $\Gamma\subset [0,+\infty)$ a DCC set. Then there exists a positive real number $\tau=\tau_{\operatorname{iglct}}(d,\Gamma)$ depending only on $d$ and $\Gamma$ satisfying the following. Let ${\mathfrak{B}}/U$ and ${\mathfrak{B}}'/U$ be two algebraically integrable normalized foliated structures of dimension $d$. Assume that
    \begin{enumerate}
    \item $X$ is the ambient variety of ${\mathfrak{B}}$ and ${\mathfrak{B}}'$ and the associated morphism $X\rightarrow U$ is a contraction, $X$ is $\mathbb Q$-factorial of Fano type over $U$, and $\rho(X/U)=1$,
